libniji C library: locale support
 libniji is an implementation of the GNU C Library's ABI (glibc $abi, x86-64).
 This package holds the locale sources under /usr/share/i18n/locales (generated
 by libniji from Unicode CLDR data, with the C.UTF-8 source), the SUPPORTED
 list of the locales they define and a set of character maps under
 /usr/share/i18n/charmaps, with the commands that use them: locale-gen
 compiles the locales /etc/locale.gen selects into /usr/lib/locale, update-locale
 sets the system's locale variables in /etc/locale.conf and validlocale says
 whether a locale is available (localedef, in libc-bin, run under those names).
